KONOHAGAKURE — HYUGA BRANCH HOUSE SEAL POLICY

The Branch House (Bunke) of the Hyuga clan bears the Caged Bird Seal (Curse Mark of the Cursed Seal Jutsu), applied to protect the Byakugan.

Provisions:
- The seal is applied to Branch House members and serves to protect the clan's Byakugan by sealing the eyes upon the bearer's death, so the kekkei genkai cannot be stolen by outsiders.
- The seal grants the Main House the ability to discipline; its use is a matter of clan tradition and internal governance.
- Reform of the seal tradition is a longstanding point of tension within the clan (see Neji Hyuga's history).

Because the seal protects a village-strategic bloodline against theft by rival villages (cf. the Hyuga Affair with the Hidden Cloud), the practice is recognized under clan law. Grievances are directed to the clan head and, where security is implicated, the Council.
Maintained by the Hyuga clan head.
